WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.310
Introduction. Our Eco-Budget mission.

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:10.765
Hey there, Year 7. Today you're going to
plan a class celebration.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:15.205
You can choose a games session, a quiz
celebration, or a recycled-art workshop.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.325
Which one would you choose? We have a
pretend budget

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.985
of 120 ringgit. We're not spending real
money today.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.460
However, you will be learning how to
organise your plan using a spreadsheet, like
last year.

00:00:28.475 --> 00:00:35.405
I've already prepared this starter table for
you, so you won't need to create one from
scratch.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:40.485
Your job today is to find the correct cells,
make four changes,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.855
and save your own copy. Our WAGBA is:

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:49.615
identify and edit information in a
spreadsheet, choose a class activity,

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.415
and save my own Eco-Budget starter in school
storage.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:01:01.825
Let's break that down so you know what
you're learning. First, our knowledge. These
are the facts I want you to remember.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:06.575
A spreadsheet contains boxes called cells.
Columns go down and use letters.

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.095
Rows go across and use numbers.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.425
When we name a cell, we say the column
letter first, followed by the row number.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:21.895
For example, B2 means column B, row 2. Next,
our skills.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:29.515
These are the things you practise doing.
You'll select a cell, replace its content
and confirm your change.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:35.195
Then you'll save your workbook and reopen it
to check that your changes are still there.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:40.545
Finally, our understanding. This is where I
want you to think about why those actions
matter.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:48.045
Imagine putting the right number beside the
wrong item. Your number might be correct,
but your plan would tell us the wrong thing.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:54.020
And imagine finishing your work, but not
knowing where you saved it.

00:01:54.035 --> 00:02:00.035
We need to check that we can find our
workbook again. That's why we'll check both
the cell address and the save location.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:06.455
You'll use three tools today. Our lesson web
app will guide you through the activities.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:12.345
Microsoft Excel is where you make changes to
your celebration plan. Your school OneDrive
is where you keep your workbook.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.115
Let me show you where to begin.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:24.765
Open Microsoft Teams and find Y7T Computer
Science 2026-2027. Select Classwork.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:31.135
Look for Week 9 Practical – Eco-Budget –
Getting Started with Excel. Open that module

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.555
and select the first link: Start Here –
Eco-Budget web app.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:41.635
You can see the heading Plan a class
celebration. Enter your name and class.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:47.695
At the top, choose English or English plus
Mandarin if you need the language support.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:50.335
Use it if it helps you understand the
instructions.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:56.405
Choose your device. If you're using an iPad,
select iPad · Excel app.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:02.965
That choice helps the web page show you the
right instructions. Now select Start /
resume my lesson.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:09.195
You'll begin with a card called Your class.
Your celebration. For now, stay in the
lesson web page.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:12.885
I'll guide you into Excel when we reach Main
task 2.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:19.365
Read one card, try the activity and check
the feedback before you continue.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:25.395
If I say Pause and look, stop typing or
tapping and look towards me. Leave your work
open.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:32.360
Remember, you don't need to rush. I want you
to understand what you're changing and check
it carefully. Let's get started.
